{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token, posts to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s events under ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device:<session>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-prefixed one, ","type":"text"},{"code":"token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"bucket","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), one of 255 properties or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it ingests none of a request’s events, and its track API ingests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only events from the last 5 days, so a record older than that when it is sent is counted as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered and not stored. A wrong region, or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing stored too, so check the project’s Live View after setting the destination up.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},